cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the benchmark it produces, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  Kayenta AI Canary Judge: a model-agnostic remote judge and benchmark for
  automated canary analysis
abstract: >-
  A configurable remote judge for Kayenta that produces a canary verdict from a
  large language model or a vision-language model, three explicit hybrid policies
  that combine it with the genuine NetflixACAJudge verdict, a tuned statistical
  ensemble baseline, and a seeded nine-family fault-injection benchmark of 180
  labelled scenarios with the harness that scores every judge over it. Version
  1.1.0 adds a documented format for labelled canary windows exported from any
  metric store, a loader, the own-data Make targets and an example file, so a
  practitioner's own windows are scored by the same code that produced the
  published results; it corrects six tools that assumed the results directory
  would always be this study's, gives each run its own figure spec, figure
  scratch directory and judge-call log directory, lets a window declare the
  order of its metrics rather than have the loader sort them by name, and
  derives each anonymised window's opaque metric suffix from a salted hash of
  the window identifier instead of its position in the sorted file. The
  benchmark scenarios, seeds, metric names, series and rubric hashes are
  generated exactly as in 1.0.0. Version 1.1.1 names the two locally built
  images explicitly, so the Make targets work from a clone in any folder, pins
  the Python dependencies of the host tools, and updates the citation metadata;
  scenarios, seeds, metric names, series and rubric hashes are unchanged.
